📊 SmartOps MIS Management System

An Excel-based Management Information System (MIS) designed to streamline operational reporting, monitor performance, track inventory, and support data-driven decision-making through interactive dashboards and automated reports.

Project Overview

SmartOps MIS Management System is a portfolio project developed using Microsoft Excel to simulate real-world business operations. It consolidates operational data into dashboards and reports, helping businesses monitor key performance indicators (KPIs), track activities, and improve reporting efficiency.

Key Features

* Master Dashboard: Consolidated overview of important operational metrics.
* FMS Dashboard: Tracks field activities, turnaround time (TAT), and performance.
* Checklist Dashboard: Monitors task completion and process compliance.
* Order Tracking: Manages order details and tracks order status.
* Inventory Management: Monitors inventory levels and stock availability.
* MIS Reporting: Supports daily, weekly, and monthly reporting.
* Data Analysis: Uses Excel formulas and analytical tools to summarize business data.
* Performance Monitoring: Helps identify pending tasks, delays, and operational issues.

Tools & Technologies

* Microsoft Excel
* Pivot Tables
* VLOOKUP and XLOOKUP
* Excel Formulas and Functions
* Conditional Formatting
* Charts and Data Visualization
* KPI Tracking and MIS Reporting

Project Objectives

* Centralize operational data in a structured workbook.
* Simplify business reporting and performance monitoring.
* Improve data visibility through interactive dashboards.
* Track task completion, inventory, and order status.
* Identify delays and operational inefficiencies.
* Support faster, data-driven business decisions.

Project Structure

The Excel workbook includes dedicated worksheets for dashboards, operational tracking, inventory management, and reporting.

Main File: SmartOps_MIS_Management_System.xlsx

How to Use

1. Download or clone this repository.
2. Open SmartOps_MIS_Management_System.xlsx in Microsoft Excel.
3. Explore the dashboards and worksheets.
4. Review the sample business data and operational metrics.
5. Update the data with your own records to explore the reporting functionality.
6. Verify formulas, charts, and dashboard calculations after modifying the data.

Note: This project uses fictional sample business data for demonstration and portfolio purposes.

